# Issue: SCC.tsort broke ties by Ord Id, which is string-intern order, so the
# let nesting in IConv, the def order in Simplify's selectSimple and the
# binding groups in TCheck's doSCC reached the .bo in first-sighting order.
# Fix: the three sites use SCC.tsortStable, which breaks ties by input position.
# Pull request: https://github.com/MatX-inc/bsc/pull/185
# Probe: LetOrder's .bo dump alone versus behind LetOrderScramble, which interns
# its names the other way; unfixed, the batched dump nests the two independent
# local bindings and orders the two top-level definitions the other way round.

batching_bo_pair LetOrder.bs LetOrderRoot.bs LetOrderScramble.bs
